./_project/codex-B2.log:324:  - `GET <formsEndpoint>?action=leads&token=<READ_TOKEN>` returns `{ok:true, headers:[…], rows:[[…]], updatedAt}`; headers are: `Timestamp, Source, Name, Phone, Specialty, Doctor, Branch, Preferred day, Preferred time, Message, Language, Page URL, Status, Notes, UTM source, UTM medium, UTM campaign, UTM content, UTM term, Click ID, Landing page, Referrer, Device, First touch`. Older rows may have fewer columns — be tolerant; look values up by header name, never by index.
./_project/codex-B2.log:325:  - `POST <formsEndpoint>` with a `text/plain` JSON body `{action:'updateStatus', token, row:<1-based sheet row>, status, notes}` updates a row. Browser POSTs to Apps Script must use `mode:'no-cors'` with `Content-Type: text/plain` (see `site/assets/js/forms.js` for the reason) — the response is opaque, so re-fetch the leads afterwards to confirm. Apps Script GETs return normal CORS-readable JSON.
